Monopsony client 1.0.0-rc2 has been installed.

To get started:

1. Copy the example config:
   cp /usr/local/etc/monopsony/client.toml.example /usr/local/etc/monopsony/client.toml
   # Edit client.toml with your server address

2. Pair with your Monopsony server:
   monopsony-client pair --server <host> --code <code>

3. Enable and start the service:
   sysrc monopsony_client_enable="YES"
   service monopsony-client start

4. Configure your package managers to use the local proxy:
   monopsony-client configure --server <host>

The local HTTP proxy listens on 127.0.0.1:3129 by default.
